# Granular — 90 bpm, D dorian. A demo of the granular engine: a grain
# cloud on one track (`automate keys.gran`) and across the whole mix bus
# (`automate gran`, no track).
#
#   beats  0-8    PLAIN   a felt-piano figure, dry
#   beats  8-16   CLOUD   the keys open into grains 0.3 s behind the
#                         playing, spread in time, pitch and space
#   beats 16-24   FREEZE  the cloud catches the chord at beat 16 and holds
#                         it, scrubbing back through what it caught, while
#                         the keys play on dry above it; a quarter of the
#                         grains run backwards
#   beats 24-32   SHIMMER the whole mix through the bus engine, an octave
#                         up, then two, sparse and wide

bpm 90
gate 0.95
tail 4

section PLAIN 0..8
section CLOUD 8..16
section FREEZE 16..24
section SHIMMER 24..32

automate reverb_wet
0.25
automate reverb_decay
0.8

track keys patch=feltkeys vel=0.8 gran_size=140 gran_density=36 gran_pos=0.3 gran_spray=0.25 gran_pan_scatter=0.9
(D3:0.5 A3:0.5 E4:0.5 F4:0.5 | C3:0.5 G3:0.5 D4:0.5 E4:0.5)x8
automate keys.gran
0 >8 0.75:2@smooth >16 1 >24 0.5
automate keys.gran_pitch_scatter
0 >8 0.15 >16 0.3
automate keys.gran_freeze
0 >16 1 >24 0
automate keys.gran_pos
0.3 >16 0.3 1.2:8@smooth
automate keys.gran_reverse
0 >16 0.25

track pad patch=aurora vel=0.6 gain=0.6
R:16 [D2 A2 F3]:8 [G2 D3 A3]:8

automate gran
0 >24 0.6
automate gran_pitch
0 >24 12 >28 24
automate gran_size
200
automate gran_density
14
automate gran_spray
0.6
automate gran_pan_scatter
1
